    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25iQL1iD5DoiTnWc6CXKb5a)_\n\n## What\n- `sp-org-ext` failed with `Recursive 'require' for feature 'sp-collection-query-book'`.\n\n## Cause\n- `sp-collection-query-book.el` ran `(with-eval-after-load 'vulpea-ui (require 'sp-collection-query-book-widget))` **before** its own `(provide ...)`.\n- `sp-org-ext` loads `vulpea-ui` before `sp-collection-query`, so the `with-eval-after-load` body ran immediately.\n- The widget file requires `sp-collection-query-book`, which was not yet provided, so the require recursed.\n\n## Fix\n- Move `(provide 'sp-collection-query-book)` above the `with-eval-after-load` block.\n- Same change in the literate source `docs/tangles/funct/sp-collection-query.org`, with a bullet explaining why.\n\n## Checked\n- All `require`/`provide` names in the `sp-collection-query*` modules match their file names; no old `vulpea-collection` module names remain in them.\n- No other cycle in the require graph.\n\n## Not tested\n- No Emacs in the cloud container, so the modules were not loaded in batch. Please start Emacs once to confirm `sp-org-ext` loads.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiB1cbJYhBZ49KEwepB)_",
